FFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-5s/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli exposes Blocked on ref rows[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-blocked[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-blocked: add an always-present `blocked` boolean to `bob ref [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list/show/find` rows (true when the note's single ^ref tracker is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Blocked [?]), document it in docs/ref.md as an overlay on the reading [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane, and test it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hotkey registry and CI render artifacts in Bob Mac Capture[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-groundwork[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-groundwork: replace the single-key HotKeyManager with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]HotKeyRegistry that routes by EventHotKeyID, keep Capture's hotkey [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]working through it, add a shared PNG render helper for design tests, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make CI render and upload design fixtures as an artifact.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]RefsCore target — decoding, item model, fetcher, and stores[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-core-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-blocked[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-core-model: add the Foundation-only RefsCore target with lossy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decoding of `bob ref list` and `bob plan` JSON, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]RefItem/RefKind/RefState/RefScope model, the BobRefsFetcher over [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BobProcessClient, the snapshot cache and open log stores, fake-bob [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref/plan branches, synthetic fixtures, and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]RefsCore ranking — browse sections, search tiers, stability, [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]explanations[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-core-ranking[dim] · [dim][/dim]after refs-core-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-core-ranking: implement browse sections, tiered search scoring with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]named constants, captions, the why-here explanation, content-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh of a frozen listing, golden tests over a synthetic library, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the refs-rank tuning CLI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Refs library service and panel model[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-panel-model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after refs-core-ranking[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-panel-model: build the RefsLibrary refresh service (cache, watcher,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]git-date pass, Today, Spotlight sweep, missing PDFs, open log) and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]RefsPanelModel (query, scope, frozen listing, selection, commands, open [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch, banners) with fake-bob tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Refs panel window, list, basic inspector, and keyboard[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-panel-ui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after refs-panel-model, mac-groundwork[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-panel-ui: build the borderless non-activating glass panel, search [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bar, two-line rows, section headers, basic inspector, footer, empty and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]error states, key router, motion and accessibility, with geometry, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]router, and rendered design tests checked from the CI artifact.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hotkeys, Highlights takeover, menu, settings, and coexistence [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]with Capture[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-entry-points[dim] · [dim][/dim]after refs-panel-ui, mac-groundwork[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-entry-points: wire the library and panel into AppDelegate, register[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the global ⌃⇧⌘R hotkey and the Highlights-frontmost takeover, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]References status-menu item and Settings section, keep only one Bob [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel visible, refresh Today after captures, and test it all.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Kind-adaptive inspector and actions menu[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-inspector[dim] · [dim][/dim]after refs-panel-ui[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-inspector: upgrade the inspector with PDFKit thumbnails or outlines[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]by kind, Bottom-line and abstract excerpts, reading-time estimates, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commented highlights from `bob ref show -c`, open history, and a ⌘K [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]actions menu, all lazy, cancellable, and cached.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]README coherence, optional memory record, final CI, and [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]Bryan's checklist[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]refs-closeout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-blocked, refs-entry-points, refs-inspector[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refs-closeout: make the README's Bob Refs section coherent, apply or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record the memory decision, confirm final CI and render fixtures, record[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proposed follow-ups, and leave Bryan a